<title>USA: Wyle says to buy back 1 mln common shares.</title>
<headline>Wyle says to buy back 1 mln common shares.</headline>
<dateline>IRVINE, Calif. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wyle Electronics said Thursday its board of directors has authorized an open-market repurchase of up to 1,000,000 shares of its common stock.</p>
<p>This plan replaces a program which was previously approved by the board in 1993. Wyle, a distributor of semiconductors, computer products and related items, has about 12.6 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The repurchased shares will be available for various corporate purposes. The program will be financed with internally generated cash and bank borrowings.</p>
</text>
